From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cuttlely vendor <vendor@cuttlely.invalid>
Date: Sat, 1 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cuttlely: git config commands

What: automatic git calls that read or check out a repository (the session snapshot, subagent and kanban worktrees, hermes -w checkout and cleanup, delegation recovery hints, worktree reclaim, and the file-picker listing) use noninteractive_repo_git_env. Fixed keys such as core.fsmonitor and core.hooksPath stay pinned, and repository-named clean, smudge, and process filters are overridden. Discovery fails closed on includeIf, more than 256 filter keys, or a config git cannot parse, and the caller skips that automatic git operation. Why: a repository's own git config can name a command that git runs during status, checkout, and branch deletion. This is NousResearch/hermes-agent pull 130661 (v0.21.6), adapted onto the f42f579 pin. UPSTREAM_COMMIT is unchanged. The website docs and the upstream tests tree are excluded from the vendor set, so those hunks are not in this patch. _worktree_is_dirty on this pin takes only the worktree path, so that probe was hardened in place.
